  "findings": [
    "The surface contains both baseline-preferred and capped-preferred regions plus tie regions; static residual suppression is conditional.",
    "For textRuneLength >= 17, the lowest structured cardinality (one feature per graph/provenance subchannel) prefers cap64 but still remains negative-margin, so stronger suppression does not guarantee recovery.",
    "At structuredPerSubchannel=2 or 4 and textRuneLength >=17, cap128 and cap64 tie on margin despite cap64 restoring substantially more local incremental dimensions.",
    "At structuredPerSubchannel=8 and textRuneLength >=17, proportional baseline is strongest even as the text/structured ratio rises from about 0.91 to 3.15.",
    "A near-equal cardinality-ratio pair (3.10 versus 3.147) prefers opposite policies, rejecting a simple single-ratio switching threshold.",
    "cap64 has the lowest mean regret among the three fixed policies on this grid, but still has max regret about 0.208; this is not evidence for a default cap64 policy."
  ],
